.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt GROWSET 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm growset
.Nd compute the sector ranges written by an ext2 grow
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -save
.Op Fl -ranges
.Op Fl -lba Ar START
.Op Fl -map Ar JSON
.Ar VOLUME SECTORS
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads the ext2 superblock and descriptors from
.Ar VOLUME
and computes the grown volume's geometry as resize2fs does, for the one
layout it accepts: 4096-byte blocks, a resize inode with enough reserved
descriptor blocks, no RAID stride, and the bitmap layout it checks.
.Ar VOLUME
is a file containing the volume, either an image or a partition copied
from a disk.
.Ar SECTORS
is the partition's size after the grow.
.Pp
The output contains one line per run of sectors written by the grow:
.Dl range START COUNT WHAT
The ranges are sorted and merged.
Sector numbers are relative to the start of the volume unless
.Fl -lba
is given.
The ranges are followed by
.Ql total SECTORS
and the grown volume's geometry.
.Pp
The host and the recovery image both compile
.Pa utils/growset.c ,
so the plan and recovery use the same calculation.
.Pa tools/dev/machine_grow.sh
compares the calculated list with the supplied ranges
before saving or writing.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -save
Include all sectors of the input volume in the calculated ranges.
The input file's length must match the volume size given by the
superblock's block count.
.It Fl -ranges
Format each range as a sector pair, without its description.
Suppress totals and geometry.
With
.Fl -map ,
the map check's results follow the pairs.
.It Fl -lba Ar START
Use disk-relative sector numbers, with the volume starting at
.Ar START .
Include the disk's first page, where growroot
rewrites the partition entry.
.It Fl -map Ar JSON
Check QEMU's written extents in
.Ar JSON
against the calculated set.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl growset --lba 266240 root.ext2 471040
.Pp
In the source tree,
.Ql tests/run grow
exercises this command.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr recovery 7 ,
.Xr growboot 8 ,
.Xr growroot 8
